{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall say to them: this is the fire-offering, etc.</b> He designated a separate act of speaking. Also, He said <b>this is the fire-offering</b>, lest they think that what HaShem commanded — a lamb, etc. — for the daily offerings is on account of sufficiency and not as a fixed measure, excluding the possibility of more than it or less than it. Therefore He designated a separate act of speaking to delimit the matter, and said ״זֶה הָאִשֶּׁה״ — this and no more than it: ״אֶת הַכֶּבֶשׂ אֶחָד״ etc. ״וְאֶת הַכֶּבֶשׂ״ etc. You thus find that in the first verse, ״צַו אֶת״ etc., they were commanded concerning the constancy of offering the daily offerings, and in this verse they were commanded concerning the measure of offering the daily offerings."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:44.309978048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}